It is Thursday morning, and my alarm rings.
I wake up and feel really terrible.
My head is heavy, and I am very tired.
I open my eyes, but they itch a lot.
It actually hurts a little when I blink.
I try to drink some water from the glass on my table.
But my throat is completely dry.
It hurts in my throat when I swallow.
I look at my phone to see what time it is.
It is half past seven, and I normally take the bus at this time.
But I have no energy at all today.
I do not just feel tired, but really sick.
I definitely ought to stay home from work today.
I write a short message to my colleague Peter.
I explain that I feel unwell and will not be coming into the office.
He replies quickly that I should just relax and get well.
I ought to call the medical clinic when they open.
But right now I just want to close my eyes and rest my heavy head.
